<Legal title="Privacy policy" effective="October 28, 2026">
    <p>
        This privacy policy tells how Synnax Labs, Inc. ("Synnax Labs", "we", "us")
        collects, uses, shares, and protects personal information. It applies when you:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Visit our websites, such as{" "}
            <a href="https://www.synnaxlabs.com">www.synnaxlabs.com</a> and{" "}
            <a href="https://docs.synnaxlabs.com">docs.synnaxlabs.com</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
            Use the Synnax portal at{" "}
            <a href="https://portal.synnaxlabs.com">portal.synnaxlabs.com</a>, where you
            manage your account and licenses.
        </li>
        <li>Use Synnax Desktop.</li>
        <li>Contact us, or deal with us in sales, support, or events.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Synnax Labs controls this information. This is also true when your organization
        gives you access to our services. If you have questions, email{" "}
        <a href="mailto:privacy@synnaxlabs.com">privacy@synnaxlabs.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        The Synnax Core, Console, and Driver that you run on your own computers do not
        send us the data that you record. A Synnax Core checks its license on its own,
        with no connection to us. The Console and Synnax Desktop check for updates, as
        section 1 tells.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Portal account</strong>: your name, email address, and password. If
            you log in with Google or Microsoft, we get your name, email address, and
            profile image from that account. We do not get your Google or Microsoft
            password. If you turn on two-step login by text message, we keep your phone
            number.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Organization</strong>: the name of your organization, its members,
            and their roles. When a person invites you to an organization, we get your
            email address from that person.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Messages</strong>: what you send us in a contact form, a feedback
            form, or an email, such as your name, email address, phone number, company,
            and message.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information about your machines and licenses</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>License records</strong>: the licenses of your organization, their
            terms and seats, and a log of license actions. The log records who did each
            action and when, and the machine names, fingerprints, and email addresses
            that the action used.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Machine names</strong>: the name that you give a machine when you
            activate a license. For Synnax Desktop, the host name of the computer.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Host fingerprints</strong>: salted, slow hashes of the hardware
            (MAC) addresses of the network interfaces of a computer. We get the hashes,
            not the addresses.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Renewals</strong>: when each Synnax Desktop computer first logged in
            and last renewed its license.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="desktop-usage-data">Synnax Desktop usage data</h3>
    <p>
        After you log in, Synnax Desktop can send usage data. It sends none before you
        log in. Usage data is linked to the email address and ID of your account, and
        holds:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Launches</strong>: a random ID for the install, the app version, the
            operating system, the processor type, and the time since the last launch.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Screens</strong>: the type of each tab that you look at, such as a
            line plot or a schematic. Not its name.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Clicks</strong>: the parts of the app that you click, with all text
            masked.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Screen recordings</strong>: recordings of the app window, which show
            what you click and how the screen changes. They show the text in the app,
            such as channel names, and what you type, but not passwords. Plots, logs,
            and values show blank.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Actions</strong>: when you create a channel, plot, schematic, or
            range, connect or configure a device, start a task, or deploy an automation.
            Types only, not names.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>The built-in Core</strong>: how long it takes to start, how long it
            ran, why it stopped, and the size of the data that a reset erased.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Crash reports</strong>: the error message and where in the app it
            occurred. An error message can name a channel or a device.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Survey answers</strong>: your answers, if you answer a survey in the
            app.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        PostHog, which stores usage data for us, also receives the IP address of the
        computer. It uses the address to find the country and city, and then discards
        it. Synnax Desktop does not send recorded data, channel values, or files. We use
        usage data to find bugs and to learn which features people use.
    </p>
    <p>
        We use the country of your IP address to choose how the login page asks about
        usage data. In the EU, the EEA, the UK, Switzerland, and countries that we
        cannot identify, it asks for your consent, and Synnax Desktop sends usage data
        only if you agree. Everywhere else, it shows a notice, and usage data is on. To
        turn usage data off at any time, run the "Change usage data settings" command in
        the app, and turn off "Share usage data".
    </p>

    <h3 id="website-analytics">Website analytics</h3>
    <p>
        On www.synnaxlabs.com, docs.synnaxlabs.com, and the portal, PostHog records the
        pages that you visit, your clicks, the page that sent you, how fast pages load,
        and your browser and device type. How it records them depends on cookies:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>With cookies</strong>: PostHog stores a cookie with a random ID in
            your browser for one year. The ID shows us when you come back, and connects
            your visits across our websites. PostHog also makes screen recordings of
            your visits, which show what you click and how the page changes. Recordings
            hide what you type in forms. In the portal, recordings hide all text.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Without cookies</strong>: PostHog stores nothing in your browser and
            makes no recordings. To count visitors, it makes a code from your IP address
            and browser type, with a random value that changes each day. It cannot
            connect the code to you.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        In the EU, the EEA, the UK, Switzerland, and countries that we cannot identify,
        our websites ask before they use cookies. They count visits without cookies
        until you choose, and after you reject. Everywhere else, they use cookies. To
        turn cookies on or off, click "Cookie settings" at the bottom of a page.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you log in to the portal while cookies are on, we link your website visits to
        your account and to your Synnax Desktop usage data. PostHog receives your IP
        address, uses it to find your country and city, and then discards it.
    </p>

    <h3>Information we collect automatically</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Search</strong>: the words that you search for in the documentation.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Updates</strong>: while they are open, the Console and Synnax
            Desktop ask our website for updates every 30 seconds, also before you log
            in. Our website sends the request on to GitHub, which serves the updates.
            Both get your IP address.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Logs</strong>: our servers and service providers record the IP
            address, browser, and time of each request, for security and to fix
            problems.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Cookies and browser storage</strong>: the portal uses cookies to
            keep you logged in and to remember the organization that you chose last. Our
            websites keep your cookie choice in a cookie for one year, and use the
            analytics cookie that "Website analytics" tells about. The documentation
            stores your display choices in your browser, such as the programming
            language of code examples. We do not use cookies for advertising.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How we use information, and our legal bases</h2>
    <p>
        We use personal information for these purposes. If the law of the EU, the EEA,
        the UK, or Switzerland applies to you, the legal basis of each purpose is in
        parentheses.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            To make and run your account and organization, to issue, renew, and check
            licenses, to count seats, and to send service emails, such as invitations
            and warnings that a license will expire (contract).
        </li>
        <li>
            To find bugs in Synnax Desktop and to learn which features people use, with
            usage data and recordings (consent).
        </li>
        <li>
            To keep our services and your account safe, to prevent abuse, such as too
            many license requests in a short time, and to keep logs (legitimate
            interests: to protect our services and our users).
        </li>
        <li>
            To learn how people use our websites, and to link their visits to their
            account, with cookies and recordings (consent).
        </li>
        <li>
            To count visits without cookies (legitimate interests: to make our websites
            and documentation better).
        </li>
        <li>
            To answer your messages and give support (legitimate interests: to answer
            you).
        </li>
        <li>
            To keep records for tax, contracts, and disputes, and to obey the law (legal
            obligation, and legitimate interests: to protect our rights).
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        To get our assessment of a legitimate interest, email{" "}
        <a href="mailto:privacy@synnaxlabs.com">privacy@synnaxlabs.com</a>. We do not
        sell personal information. We do not share it for targeted advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Who we share information with</h2>
    <p>
        These service providers process personal information for us, under contracts
        that limit how they use it:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Clerk</strong>: portal accounts, login, and organizations. Clerk
            also sends login, invitation, and password emails and text messages. When
            you make an account, Clerk can use Cloudflare Turnstile to check that you
            are not a bot.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>PostHog</strong> (US cloud): Synnax Desktop usage data, website
            analytics, and recordings.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Vercel</strong>: hosts our websites and the portal. It finds your
            country from your IP address, so that our websites and the login page know
            whether to ask before they use cookies or usage data.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Neon</strong>: stores portal records in a database.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Resend</strong>: sends emails that a license will expire.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Amazon Web Services</strong>: signs license keys. The signed data
            includes host fingerprints and the ID of your organization.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Formspree</strong>: receives contact and feedback forms.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Algolia</strong>: runs the documentation search, and gets the words
            that you search for and your IP address.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>DigitalOcean</strong>: serves the images and videos on our websites.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>GitHub</strong>: serves updates for the Console and Synnax Desktop.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Google and Microsoft get information only if you log in with them. We can also
        share information when the law requires it, to protect our rights, or as part of
        a merger, sale, or similar change of our company. No other company collects
        information about your activity across other websites through our services.
    </p>

    <h2>4. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
        We are in the United States. When you use our services from the EU, the EEA, the
        UK, or Switzerland, you send your information to us in the United States. We are
        not certified under the Data Privacy Framework.
    </p>
    <p>
        Our service providers in the United States get your information under one of
        these safeguards:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Their certification under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, its UK
            Extension, or the Swiss-U.S. Data Privacy Framework.
        </li>
        <li>
            The standard contractual clauses of the European Commission (Decision (EU)
            2021/914), with the UK Addendum and the Swiss changes.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        To get a copy of a safeguard, email{" "}
        <a href="mailto:privacy@synnaxlabs.com">privacy@synnaxlabs.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How long we keep information</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Account and organization information</strong>: while your account is
            open. When you ask us to delete it, we delete it within 30 days, with the
            Synnax Desktop usage data and recordings linked to it. Copies in backups
            expire within 30 days after that. We keep license records as the next item
            tells.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>License records</strong>, with their machine names and fingerprints:
            for the life of the license and 7 years after it ends, for contracts, tax,
            and disputes.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Synnax Desktop usage data</strong>: 25 months after you last use
            Synnax Desktop. Recordings of the app window: 30 days.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Website analytics</strong>: 25 months. Recordings of website visits:
            30 days.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Server logs</strong>: 30 days.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Messages</strong>: as long as we need them to answer you, and 3
            years after.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. How we protect information</h2>
    <p>
        We encrypt connections to our services, limit who can get access to personal
        information, and keep the license signing key in a hardware key service. The
        portal gets only hashes of network addresses, never the addresses. No system is
        completely secure, so we cannot promise that information will never be lost or
        stolen. If a security incident puts your information at risk, we tell you and
        the authorities as the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <h3>Your right to object</h3>
    <p>
        You can object at any time to our use of your information based on legitimate
        interests. Email{" "}
        <a href="mailto:privacy@synnaxlabs.com">privacy@synnaxlabs.com</a>. We then
        stop, unless we have strong legal grounds to continue, or we need the
        information for legal claims.
    </p>
    <h3>Your other rights</h3>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you can also have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Get a copy of the personal information we have about you.</li>
        <li>Correct information that is wrong.</li>
        <li>Delete your information.</li>
        <li>
            Get your information in a format that you can move to a different service.
        </li>
        <li>Limit how we use your information.</li>
        <li>Withdraw your consent, with no effect on what we did before.</li>
        <li>Complain to your data protection authority.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Residents of California and other US states can have the right to know, correct,
        and delete their information, and to opt out of its sale or sharing. We do not
        sell or share personal information. We do not treat you differently when you use
        these rights.
    </p>
    <h3>How to use your rights</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Email <a href="mailto:privacy@synnaxlabs.com">privacy@synnaxlabs.com</a>. We
            can ask you to confirm who you are. Another person can make a request for
            you, and we can ask for proof of your permission.
        </li>
        <li>
            We answer within one month. For a complex request, we can take two more
            months, and we tell you if we need them.
        </li>
        <li>
            To stop Synnax Desktop usage data, turn off "Share usage data" in the app.
        </li>
        <li>
            To turn off website cookies, click "Cookie settings" at the bottom of a page
            of our websites.
        </li>
        <li>
            To remove a Synnax Desktop computer from your account, log it out on the
            Devices page of the portal.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        If you are in the UK, you can complain to us first. We confirm that we got your
        complaint within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Information you must give</h2>
    <p>
        You must give an email address to make an account or to get a license. Without
        it, we cannot give you an account. All other information is optional. We do not
        make decisions about you based only on automated processing that have legal or
        similarly significant effects.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Children</h2>
    <p>
        Our services are not for people under 18. We do not knowingly collect
        information from them. If you think that we have such information, email us and
        we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>
        Our websites do not change what they do when a browser sends a Do Not Track
        signal.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        When we change this policy, we change the effective date at the top. If a change
        is important, we tell account holders by email before it applies.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:privacy@synnaxlabs.com">privacy@synnaxlabs.com</a>, or
        write to:
    </p>
    <p>
        Synnax Labs, Inc.
